{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/84688-what-was-your-first-monster-hunt","id":84688,"title":"What was your first 'monster' hunt?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-05T10:21:02-08:00","id":84688,"title":"What was your first 'monster' hunt?","content":"I would like to hear some of your first, or the first, monsters your hunters have fought as PC or ST. Mine was a biotech zombie In New York City, five days before Christmas.(The Game was nicknamed 'Five Days Before Christmas') The game started in an apartment complex were the hunters (more like mortals at the start) held the apartment complex and did what they could for the others in the apartment (run out for drugs, lots of interactions with the NPCs in the complex, start up the back up generator, ete) If the zombies bit you, it was a chance die to be immune (10%), stamina decided how long one lasted. After a few days (PCs had to live til Christmas) the cause of the biozombies showed up, a white humanoid with long skinny limps, sharp teeth, very fast and shrugged off bullets. It caused a number of floors to become overrun and loved to hit and run. All in all a good game, most of the PCs lived to see the end due to using their heads and good luck. How did they take care of the first zombie? They blocked the glass door the moment they saw a creepy homeless man trying to open the pull doors without the use of its hands...the White Zombie as the hunters called it, met its end on the last day after being tracked down. The hunters had its head cut off, remains burned, bones crushed, salted, and burnt again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2436-cold-cross","name":"Cold Cross","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}